    "liveness": "os.kill(pid, 0) / os.killpg(pgid, 0) inspection only; EPERM counts as alive; no signal is ever delivered (R-N11)",
    "lock": "<receipt dir>/resume.lock created O_EXCL with {pid, acquired_at}; dead-PID lock replaced atomically and recorded stale_taken_over; unreadable lock refused as resume_lock_held; removed on exit by the owning PID",
    "implementation_decisions": [
      "Rerun stages are marked status pending_resume_rerun (not success-terminal) at the first resume save, so a crash during a resume can never leave a verified-looking stage downstream of a rerun one; the superseded optional selector is kept in the pending entry for displacement.",
      "resume_index is 1-based; displaced outputs go to <run_dir>/demo-invocations/<id>/resume-<n>/displaced/<run-relative path> and are moved by rename, re-hashed and recorded; nothing is deleted.",
      "Existing-run mode: a rerun stage output whose bytes equal the verified prior snapshot is left for the unchanged OVERWRITTEN_OUTPUTS retirement (bytes are already archived); any other output is displaced. Stages marked skipped_dependency_failed during a resume also have their outputs displaced.",
      "Media success-terminal without a pointer (crash between media and pointer write) reuses stages.media.result.run_dir.",
      "A worker-run stage without recorded worker_sha256 or artifacts is rerun (reason worker_hash_unrecorded / artifacts_unrecorded), not skipped.",
      "Every invocation records resume_arguments (analysis_python stored resolved), orchestrator {pid, started_at}, resource_limits (stage timeouts, 2 MiB stream cap, memory_ceiling_bytes null, memory_ceiling_status unknown_not_measured) and per-stage started_at/completed_at/artifacts. Worker PID is checkpointed when the worker starts (invoke keyword-only on_started).",
      "Parser defaults for --profile/--backend/--features/--pitch-seconds became None and are filled after parsing (same effective defaults) so --resume conflicts are detectable.",
      "tests/test_demo.py existing fake_invoke gained an on_started=None parameter; no existing assertion changed."
    ]
  },
